## ⚙️ Setting Up My Environment
 
Before writing any code, I prepared my development environment. A properly configured environment makes programming much easier: Python is installed correctly, commands work from the terminal, and scripts can be written, edited, and run without nasty surprises.
 
I learned quickly that a few extra minutes of setup saves a lot of troubleshooting later. Problems like Python not being recognised by Windows, missing libraries, or files saved in the wrong place are usually caused by skipping an important installation step.
 
### Step 1: Download Python for Windows
 
I visited the official Python website at **python.org** instead of downloading Python from a third-party site. The site detected that I was on Windows 11 and recommended the latest stable release of Python 3. I downloaded the Windows installer and waited for the download to finish completely before opening it.


**Why I did this:** Python is the one thing every project depends on, so I wanted a trustworthy copy.
 
**What it accomplishes:** It gives me the Python interpreter, the program that reads my code and runs it.
 
**How it works:** The official site detects your operating system and offers the right installer.
 
**Why it matters in production:** Downloading software only from official sources protects against tampered installers and means I will receive official updates. The latest stable version also brings security updates and compatibility improvements without the instability of experimental releases.
 
**If skipped or done wrong:** A copy from an unofficial website could be modified or outdated, which is a real security risk.
 
### Step 2: Install Python
 
I launched the installer and carefully read the first screen before clicking anything. One option stood out as especially important:
 
```text
Add python.exe to PATH
```
 
I made sure this checkbox was **ticked**, then clicked **Install Now**, which installs Python using the recommended default settings. The installer copied the files, configured Windows, and finished within a few minutes.
 
