After installation, VS Code enabled several Python tools:
 
- Intelligent code completion (IntelliSense)
- Automatic syntax checking
- Code navigation
- Built-in debugging tools
- Python interpreter selection
- One-click program execution
- Improved terminal integration
I found IntelliSense especially useful. As I typed, VS Code suggested keywords, functions, variables, and methods, so I wrote code faster with fewer typos. The extension also underlines problems before I run the program, which makes syntax errors much easier to find.
 
### Step 6: Create My Project Folder
 
Before writing any code, I created a dedicated folder named `python-practice` on my desktop. I then opened VS Code and chose **File → Open Folder**, and selected the `python-practice` directory. The folder appeared in the **Explorer** panel on the left side of the VS Code window.
 
