**Why I did this:** Keeping everything in one place has clear advantages:
 
1. Projects are easier to find later.
2. Related files stay organised together.
3. Opening a whole folder lets VS Code manage all the project files at once instead of one at a time.
From this point on, every script in this repository is saved inside this folder.
 
> [!TIP]
> A consistent folder structure looks like a small detail, but it is good professional practice. Organised projects are easier to manage, easier to back up, and much simpler to revisit.
 
